 actually designed by  canada post like this  legitimate sir john a mcdonald stamp  this is from 2015  marked the bicentennial of his birth 1.5  million copies were printed up  but if you had a favorite photo and you  wanted to put that on a sheet of 50  stamps  it could would only cost you about 120  bucks but people have used that  vanity program for political and social  protest  back in 2006 frank magazine did that  printed up a few stamps one with a  disney character another was someone  wearing a nazi uniform and  back in the late 70s opponents of pierre  elliott trudeau  distributed what are called overprint  stamps you can see the words  fuddle duddle and r-i-p-p-e-t that were  over printed on actual canada post  stamps now  none of these are very valuable to  collectors you might find copies on ebay  for a few bucks these days but  canada post takes this very seriously  and they are now  reviewing their processes to make sure  that no stamp with an inappropriate  image ends up in your mailbox robin  david aiken in ottawa thanks david  still ahead the audition for answers to  solve live theater's pandemic problems  well they are topics we don't normally  hear the pope wing in on  in a new book of interviews the pontiff  refers to food and sex  as gifts from god that are simply divine  pope francis says the pleasure of eating  is there to keep you healthy and  sexual pleasure is there to make love  more beautiful and guarantee the  perpetuation of the species  he adds overzealous views on so-called  carnal sins that deny pleasure  have caused enormous harm covet 19 has  forced many companies to change the way  they do business  but there are some industries that are  in a prolonged intermission  live theater needs a packed house to be  profitable but as mike drolla explains  the seats are empty  this is the heart of canada's vibrant  theater scene  for six months its old heartbeat has  been missing  [Music]  live theater like sporting events and  concerts is 